    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PAA\nConquest\nof the Pacific\n1934\nFIRST US. NAVY SQUADRON FLIGHT - SAN FRANCISCO TO HAWAII\nAAMC *1-0 1200\nIDP)\nLT. COR KNEFFLER MCGINNIS,\nWITH HIS MASSED FLIGHT OF SIX\nCONSOLIDATED PZY-/ PATROL\nBOATS, FLEW NONSTOR FROM\nSAN FRANCISCO TO HAWAIL AS A\nROUTINE TRANSFER TO THEIR\nNEW BASE AT PEARL HARBOR.\nIN THE 24% - HOUR, 2400 - MHE\nFLIGHT, THEY SET THREE NEW\nWORLD RECORDS.\nCONSOLIDATED NAVY PATROL P¿Y-1.\nLead plane on the Navy's record flight to Honolulu soon after sighting the Haw\nIslands.",
      "OCT 6 - 1933\norona Cal\n1\nMARRES\nWRON\n1371\n1934\nThis envelope approved by the U.S. Post Office Dept., for AIR MAIL ONLY.\nUse for other purposes not permitted.\nHarry OT. Sweet\n6/ p",
      "H'LOWN\nthe 10-P-4,\nBy\nma tilot.\nLe Clike. 00-720.\nU.S.N.\nON MASSED FLIGHT OF\nTENTH PATROL SQUADRON,\nU.S.NAVY.\nSan Francisco, California,\nto fearl Harbor, Hawaii.\nAIRCRAFT\nBASE\n10 l\nFORCE,\n1934\nA.M.\nVV\nS. FLEE\n05937\nRex O. Copp\n1933 NORTH 14th ST.\nKansas Cily, Kansas"
    ],
